.SH FILES
.I "Table B-1. What conn reads and writes"
.RS
.TP
\fB~/.config/conn/config.json\fR
the configuration; Section 9
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/tmux\-<uid>.sock\fR
the socket the shells are held on
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/tmux.conf\fR
configuration conn writes for itself at every launch
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/latest\-release\fR
the latest release as last checked, and when
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/runs.jsonl\fR
each run of an entry's or a task's command, one per line — the command, its
name, how it ended, when, and how long it took; cut back to the last two
thousand as it grows. The heading's past runs and the finder's last runs are
read from it
.TP
\fB~/.local/state/conn/finder.json\fR
the finder's listing, everything openable, rewritten by conn whenever it changes
so the popup opens at once
.TP
\fB.conn\fR
a project's plan; Section 6
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.I "Table C-1. Variables conn reads"
.RS
.TP
\fBCONN_SOCKET\fR
where the shells are held, instead of the state directory
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
where the configuration lives, instead of ~/.config
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
where the state directory is, instead of ~/.local/state
.TP
\fBSHELL\fR
the shell \fBs\fR opens, and the one behind \fBa\fR, \fBr\fR, the tasks and a
resumed conversation
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
set, conn draws without color, as no-color.org asks; CLICOLOR_FORCE and
TERM=dumb are honored too
.TP
\fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR
where Claude Code's session files are read from, instead of ~/.claude
.TP
\fBOLLAMA_MODELS\fR
where ollama's models are read from, instead of ~/.ollama/models
.RE
